# LF everywhere, enforced in the repository.
#
# This matters more than usual here: every .sh in this repo runs inside the WSL
# Linux guest, and a shell script checked out with CRLF has a broken shebang --
# `/usr/bin/env bash\r` is not a file, and the error you get ("no such file or
# directory" for a file that plainly exists) sends you looking in the wrong
# place entirely. On a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true that happens
# silently at checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell is run by Windows but tolerates LF, so it is included above for
# consistency rather than excluded.

# Keep binary-ish things untouched should any ever arrive.
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary
